generate_dataset.py
    Generates a synthetic dataset (one fictional user, "user_001") as CSV files in data/. It does not read from the database.

train_model_from_csv.py
    Trains the machine learning model using the dataset and saves the model and encoders to be used in model.py.

model.py
    Loads the trained model and provides prediction and training functions (AI engine).

app.py
    This is the API layer. It exposes AI as an API. FastAPI service that exposes the AI model via HTTP endpoints (/predict, /train).

Local setup (temporary: the backend stops calling this service in roadmap step 6)
    Python 3.10 (as in CI). From the repository root:

        python -m venv .venv
        .venv\Scriptsctivate            (Windows; on Linux/macOS: source .venv/bin/activate)
        pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt
        pytest

    To run the service for the backend (AIService:BaseUrl defaults to http://localhost:8000):

        set AI_PREDICT_API_KEY=<same value as the backend's AIService:PredictApiKey>
        uvicorn app:app --port 8000

    Without AI_PREDICT_API_KEY every /predict call is rejected, and the backend shows no
    attendance predictions.
